# Lab Canvas — Node Editing with Inline Sidebar Panel

Improve the visual canvas ("Análise") so that clicking a node opens an inline editing panel on the right sidebar instead of a modal dialog. This keeps the canvas visible, provides a richer editing experience, and allows future extensibility (rich text, file upload, etc.).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Breaking UX change**: The modal editing flow is being replaced by a sidebar panel. The modal HTML/JS will be fully removed. If you want to keep the modal as a secondary option (e.g. for mobile), please let me know before I proceed.

> [!NOTE]
> The sidebar currently only shows the concept repository. With this change, clicking a node will replace the sidebar content with the node editor, and a "← Voltar" button returns to the repository view.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Análise Module (core canvas logic)

#### [MODIFY] [analise.js](file:///c:/Users/Warlison%20Abreu/Desktop/CODIGOS/PESSOAL/ESTUDA-TRADER/js/analise.js)

1. **Remove modal HTML** from the [renderAnalise()](file:///c:/Users/Warlison%20Abreu/Desktop/CODIGOS/PESSOAL/ESTUDA-TRADER/js/analise.js#76-165) template (lines 136-139) — delete the `#pa-modal` div entirely.

2. **Remove modal functions** — delete [openModal()](file:///c:/Users/Warlison%20Abreu/Desktop/CODIGOS/PESSOAL/ESTUDA-TRADER/js/analise.js#771-860) (lines 771-858) and [closeModal()](file:///c:/Users/Warlison%20Abreu/Desktop/CODIGOS/PESSOAL/ESTUDA-TRADER/js/analise.js#861-869) (lines 861-868) and the `closeTimeout` variable (line 769).

3. **Add sidebar state** — extend `state` object with:
   - `sidebarView: 'repository'` — tracks whether sidebar shows `'repository'` or `'editor'`
   - `editingNodeId: null` — which node is being edited

4. **New function `openNodeEditor(nodeId)`** — replaces [openModal](file:///c:/Users/Warlison%20Abreu/Desktop/CODIGOS/PESSOAL/ESTUDA-TRADER/js/analise.js#771-860):
   - Sets `state.sidebarView = 'editor'` and `state.editingNodeId = nodeId`
   - Opens the sidebar if collapsed
   - On mobile, opens sidebar overlay
   - Calls [renderSidebarContent(sidebarEl)](file:///c:/Users/Warlison%20Abreu/Desktop/CODIGOS/PESSOAL/ESTUDA-TRADER/js/analise.js#926-1015) which will detect the view mode

5. **New function `closeNodeEditor()`** — returns to repository:
   - Sets `state.sidebarView = 'repository'` and `state.editingNodeId = null`
   - Calls [renderSidebarContent(sidebarEl)](file:///c:/Users/Warlison%20Abreu/Desktop/CODIGOS/PESSOAL/ESTUDA-TRADER/js/analise.js#926-1015)

6. **Modify [renderSidebarContent(sidebar)](file:///c:/Users/Warlison%20Abreu/Desktop/CODIGOS/PESSOAL/ESTUDA-TRADER/js/analise.js#926-1015)** — add a branch at the start:
   - If `state.sidebarView === 'editor'`, call a new `renderNodeEditorPanel(sidebar)` function instead of the repository HTML
   - Otherwise, render the existing repository content (no change)

7. **New function `renderNodeEditorPanel(sidebar)`** — renders the editor form inline:
   - Header: "← Voltar" button + node title
   - Concept info (category, subcategory, prerequisite, notes) displayed as read-only
   - Textarea for comments/annotations (same as current modal)
   - Image URL input with live preview (same as current modal, only for non-image nodes)
   - For image nodes: shows the image with caption editing
   - Delete button (bottom, red)
   - Save button (primary, blue)
   - All styled with the same Tailwind classes to match the sidebar aesthetic

8. **Modify node click handler** (line 678-680):
   - Change [openModal(node.id)](file:///c:/Users/Warlison%20Abreu/Desktop/CODIGOS/PESSOAL/ESTUDA-TRADER/js/analise.js#771-860) → `openNodeEditor(node.id)`

9. **Add visual selection highlight**: when a node is being edited, add a ring/glow class to that node's DOM element (e.g. `ring-2 ring-blue-500`).

---

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification

Since this is a pure frontend UI change with no automated tests in the project, verification must be done visually in the browser:

1. **Start the dev server** — open a terminal in the project root and run `npx live-server` (or your preferred dev method), then navigate to the app in the browser.

2. **Navigate to the "Análise" tab** via the sidebar navigation.

3. **Test: Node click opens sidebar editor**
   - Drag a concept from the right sidebar onto the canvas
   - Click the node — the sidebar should switch from the repository view to the editor panel
   - Verify the editor shows: back button, node title, category info, comments textarea, image URL input

4. **Test: Save works**
   - Type text in the comments textarea
   - Enter an image URL
   - Click "Salvar" — verify a toast appears and the node is updated on the canvas

5. **Test: Back button returns to repository**
   - Click "← Voltar" — sidebar should return to the concept repository view
   - Verify the "Evolução / Operações" toggle, search, and categories are all visible again

6. **Test: Delete node from editor**
   - Click a node to open the editor
   - Click "Excluir Nó" — confirm the prompt
   - Verify the node is removed from the canvas AND the sidebar returns to the repository

7. **Test: Selection highlight**
   - Click a node — verify it gets a visual ring/highlight
   - Click "Voltar" or click another node — verify the previous highlight is removed

8. **Test: Mobile behavior**
   - Resize browser to < 768px
   - Click the sidebar toggle button — sidebar slides in
   - Click a node — sidebar should show the editor
   - Click "Voltar" — should return to repository without closing the sidebar

9. **Test: No modal remnants**
   - Verify that no modal overlay appears at any point
   - Inspect the DOM — confirm there is no `#pa-modal` element
